Some items can take more than one kind of damage - for instance,
cloaks can both burn and rot. Metal items may rust (from water) and
corrode (from acid). Leather or cloth items can both burn (from fire)
and rot (from certain pudding attacks).

However, it takes only ONE reading of a non-cursed scroll of enchant
armour/weapon while confused, and the item will be protected against
ALL forms of damage. Fireproof, rotproof, rustproof, corrodeproof, all
are the same - the item is protected against EVERYTHING. If your
gloves are fireproof, they are rotproof automatically: if your metal
weapon is rustproof, it is corrodeproof too.

